<p>In the latest development, a fifth member of Iran’s women’s soccer delegation has withdrawn her asylum claim in Australia and left the country. That leaves two of the original asylum seekers still in Australia. Reuters-based reporting said she is expected to rejoin the rest of the squad in Malaysia after leaving Australia late Sunday. The asylum requests followed fears that some team members could face persecution if they returned to Iran after staying silent during the national anthem at a Women’s Asian Cup match earlier this month.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/Rnc0AqkfLZBFvJksoJf73fQptKt0vfMvhXtfhAQFWY4BcNqGv1oIYPUb7YX_Z4-2BkIWIXBZIzrK50t65-WYcwlq92rCwCCAXyEwrxbdq_j0eIXY6GTMuwA7HEdckwacPu4JneFZhrVTPepjcW7VxbLSRjFs3ZlqvTJH4lLf4ZmK9C_aKm9X1uB9xtiTN62SOtTpnAg4EadsFLb2RXFH9YLReTPe1dCudohcBl2l' alt='Members of Iran’s women’s soccer team during the Asian Cup period linked to the asylum story' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Status in Australia: PBS and DW said the delegation members who later reversed course had already accepted refugee visas or been granted asylum in Australia.</li><li>Delegation makeup: Reuters said the asylum seekers included a support staff member as well as players.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Iranian authorities: Iranian officials accused Australia of pressuring members of the delegation to stay in the country rather than return with the team. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/iran-says-womens-football-captain-withdraws-australia-asylum-bid'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Former player and Iran International: A former Iranian player and the Persian-language channel Iran International said some players faced pressure to abandon their asylum claims through threats against family members in Iran. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/asia/australasia/article/3346688/iran-says-womens-football-captain-has-withdrawn-australia-asylum-bid'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Australian government: Australian authorities publicly confirmed the latest departure, saying the player had left the country after earlier receiving permission to stay. (<a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/fifth-member-of-iranian-womens-soccer-team-gives-up-asylum-in-australia'>PBS NewsHour</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/fifth-member-of-iranian-womens-soccer-team-gives-up-asylum-in-australia'>Fifth member of Iranian women&#x27;s soccer team gives up asylum in Australia</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/03/fifth-member-iran-womens-soccer-team-withdraws-asylum-claim'>Fifth member of Iran women&#x27;s soccer team withdraws asylum claim</a> - al-monitor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/iran-says-womens-football-captain-withdraws-australia-asylum-bid'>Iran says women’s football captain withdraws Australia asylum bid</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/03/16/g-s1-113899/5th-member-of-iranian-womens-soccer-team-gives-up-asylum-in-australia'>5th member of Iranian women&#x27;s soccer team gives up asylum in Australia</a> - npr.org</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/asia/australasia/article/3346688/iran-says-womens-football-captain-has-withdrawn-australia-asylum-bid'>Iran says women’s football captain has withdrawn Australia asylum bid</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/iran-says-women-s-soccer-captain-drops-australia-asylum-bid/a-76367156'>Iran says women&#x27;s soccer captain drops Australia asylum bid</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c98gz372683o'>Iran captain latest footballer to drop asylum bid, Iranian state media says</a> - bbc.com</li></ul>